Check that /novcautodetect is accepted and changes nothing: lld-link does not
search for Visual Studio by default, while explicit /winsysroot, /vctoolsdir
and /libpath keep working. The default and /vcautodetect are in vcautodetect.test.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.dir && mkdir -p %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64

Explicit /winsysroot is still honored.
# RUN: lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect /winsysroot:%t.dir/sysroot \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

Explicit /vctoolsdir is still honored.
# RUN: lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect \
# RUN:   /vctoolsdir:%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=FOUND %s

FOUND: VC toolchain: {{.*}}sysroot{{[/\\]}}VC{{[/\\]}}Tools{{[/\\]}}MSVC{{[/\\]}}1.1.1.1

With /novcautodetect the environment is not consulted, and no VC toolchain or
SDK path is detected at all.
# RUN: env -u LIB VCToolsInstallDir=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   not lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect /defaultlib:std64 \
# RUN:   /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONE --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="SDK lib path:" \
# RUN:     --implicit-check-not="UCRT lib path:" %s

NONE: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

/libpath still works with /novcautodetect.
# RUN: lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /novcautodetect \
# RUN:   /libpath:%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe

/winsdkdir alone adds the Windows SDK lib path with no VC toolchain, and std64.lib
is found there. (Verbose lines are only printed on a successful link here.)
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir/sdk/Include/10.0.1.1 %t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64
# RUN: cp %p/Inputs/std64.lib %t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64
# RUN: env -u LIB lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe /verbose 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=SDK --implicit-check-not="VC toolchain:" %s

SDK: Windows SDK lib path: {{.*}}sdk{{[/\\]}}Lib{{[/\\]}}10.0.1.1{{[/\\]}}um

With /winsdkdir alone and LIB set, LIB is ignored as the flag asks. That is
not a warning: a /WX link still succeeds and prints nothing.
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir/empty
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk /WX \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe > %t.wx.txt 2>&1
# RUN: count 0 < %t.wx.txt

/verbose names the flag that made lld-link ignore LIB.
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk /verbose \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=IGN-SDK %s
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /verbose \
# RUN:   /vctoolsdir:%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=IGN-VC %s
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /verbose /winsysroot:%t.dir/sysroot \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=IGN-ROOT %s
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /verbose /lldignoreenv \
# RUN:   /libpath:%t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=IGN-ENV %s

IGN-SDK: ignoring LIB: /winsdkdir given
IGN-VC: ignoring LIB: /vctoolsdir given
IGN-ROOT: ignoring LIB: /winsysroot given
IGN-ENV: ignoring LIB: /lldignoreenv given

An empty LIB is no LIB: nothing is reported as ignored.
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB= -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk /verbose \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=SDK --implicit-check-not="ignoring" %s

A library missing with /winsdkdir alone and LIB set: the note names the flag
that made lld-link ignore LIB.
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:nosuch /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=LIBNOTE %s

LIBNOTE: LINK : note: LIB is not searched because /winsdkdir was given; name the other library directories with /libpath or /vctoolsdir
LIBNOTE-NEXT: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'nosuch.lib' was not found

No note with /libpath (the user names the directories), with /lldignoreenv
(ignoring LIB is the request) or with a VC toolchain from /vctoolsdir.
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk \
# RUN:   /libpath:%t.dir/empty /defaultlib:nosuch /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONOTE --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkdir:%t.dir/sdk /lldignoreenv \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:nosuch /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONOTE --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj \
# RUN:   /vctoolsdir:%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:nosuch /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=NONOTE --implicit-check-not="LINK : note" %s

NONOTE: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'nosuch.lib' was not found

/winsdkversion alone makes lld-link ignore LIB too (as upstream; see
winsysroot.test), and is named the same way.
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/empty -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkversion:10.0.1.1 /verbose \
# RUN:   /libpath:%t.dir/sdk/Lib/10.0.1.1/um/x64 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=IGN-SDKVER %s
# RUN: not %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /winsdkversion:10.0.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck --check-prefix=LIBNOTE-SDKVER %s

IGN-SDKVER: ignoring LIB: /winsdkversion given
LIBNOTE-SDKVER: LINK : note: LIB is not searched because /winsdkversion was given; name the other library directories with /libpath or /vctoolsdir
LIBNOTE-SDKVER-NEXT: LINK : fatal error LNK1181: input file 'std64.lib' was not found

/vctoolsversion alone resolves no toolchain and does not suppress LIB.
# RUN: %python %p/Inputs/scrub-env.py LIB=%t.dir/sysroot/VC/Tools/MSVC/1.1.1.1/lib/x64 -- \
# RUN:   lld-link %p/Inputs/hello64.obj /vctoolsversion:1.1.1.1 \
# RUN:   /defaultlib:std64 /entry:main /out:%t.exe
